# Regression pin for the CONSERVATIVE side of the automatic `'actor` -> `'atomic`
# promotion pass (Part 2, see docs/qualifiers.md's `'atomic` section): `counter` is
# used inside a `with` block — criterion 4 (never used inside a `with` block) fails,
# so the promotion pass must NOT fire here; `counter` stays on the original `'actor`
# (Mutex-backed) representation.
#
# Now mutates inside the `with` block (`counter += 5`) — this used to have to stay
# read-only here: a scalar `'actor`/`'guard` binding's own assignment was never
# specially handled the way a struct field's is (see `emit_expr.rs`'s
# `emit_expr_assign`, which used to only special-case `Field` write targets through
# the lock, never a bare `Var` target) — fixed, see `var_lock_scalar`'s doc comment
# on the `Transpiler` struct (`src/transpiler/mod.rs`) and
# tests/cases/actor_guard_scalar_mutation.br for the dedicated regression coverage.
# This fixture pins down exactly one thing: that criterion 4 really does suppress
# promotion, and the (now mutating) result is still correct. See
# atomic_promotion_actor.br for the mutating, successfully-promoted counterpart, and
# `tests/atomic_qualifier.rs`'s `promotion_suppressed_for_with_block_usage` for the
# codegen-level inspection (confirms it really did stay on Mutex, not just that
# stdout happens to match).
def main():
    var counter'actor = 3
    with counter:
        counter += 5
        print "{counter}"
